{
  "_notes": [
    "age_terms: words that mean a child, an age group or a size or height standing in for age, in English, Hindi, Marathi, Bengali, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Gujarati, Malayalam, Punjabi and Urdu, in their scripts and in common Latin spellings; any of them makes a request a cannot. age_stems are the same in scripts whose words take endings (குழந்தைகள், ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು): they match at the start of a word. Adult age words (old man, elderly, senior citizen) are not age words.",
    "Text and words are folded before matching (agent/compiler.py _norm): NFKC (fullwidth letters), digits of any script to 0 to 9, the virama and nukta of Indic scripts dropped and chandrabindu read as anusvara (so बचचा is बच्चा and लडकी is लड़की), one form of Arabic script letters, zero width characters dropped, and separators inside a word dropped (a CH-ILD, a k-i-d), and spaced out single letters joined (c h i l d).",
    "boy and girl usually mean a child, so they count. Job titles that use them for adults (delivery boy, building boy) and other phrases that only look like age words (baby blue, youth hostel) are in not_age_phrases and never count.",
    "A zone or line name with an age word in it is a place only when the age word sits directly before place words and nothing else is in the name, except a possessive (बच्चों का पार्क) and a trailing number or letter (kids play area 2). Otherwise it is refused (it says who, not where). Only such names, and enrolled staff names, are masked before the check.",
    "age_patterns catch age written out: N or a number word before year, yr, yrs, yo or y/o (7-year-old, 8 yrs, a 5 y/o) unless an object follows (a 2 year old car), aged N, N years of age, under N years, under-12s and u18 (an age group, not a block or tower code: U1 parking, Tower U2), under, below, younger than, not yet, over or about N after a person (someone under 18, a person about 7, looks under 13), in their single digits or teens, N saal ka and पाँच साल का, class 5 student and 5th grader, and heights: a number and a length unit about a person (a person 110cm, about 1 metre, less than a metre, 4 feet tall) or any comparison of height (shorter than the pool railing). Counts (a group of 5, a crowd of 20), durations (kept for 7 years, under 5 minutes) and distances (2 metres from the gate) are not ages. <NAME> is one of age_pattern_parts.",
    "minor and teen count only as people: the minor gate and teen log (Hinglish, three people) do not.",
    "student alone is allowed, since college students are adults; school student, school uniform, class 5 student and the like count.",
    "child_anchors and ordinary_anchors drive the meaning check (agent/meaning.py): a looks_like or zone_looks_like text is refused when the image model's text tower puts it nearer its nearest child anchor than its nearest ordinary anchor by Tuning signals.child_meaning_margin. The calibration is in backend/tests/test_age_guard.py.",
    "age_safe_summaries: what the AI check's summary becomes when its words are about age or children (agent/verifier.py).",
    "faces_entry_*: watches about who someone is (known, unknown or one staff member) run only on entry cameras, the purposes in readers.json faces.purposes; anywhere else the AI's watch becomes one about anyone, with a cannot."
  ],
